esp_codec_dev 1.5.11: esp_codec_dev_open() fails when the data interface set_fmt fails

Upstream ignores the return value of data_if->set_fmt(). When the I2S slot
reconfiguration fails (typically ESP_ERR_NO_MEM allocating DMA descriptors in internal
RAM) the channel is left with dma.desc == NULL and the following enable() panics in
i2s_rx_channel_start with a NULL load. With this patch the open returns
ESP_CODEC_DEV_DRV_ERR and clears the opened flags, so the caller can report
"codec busy / out of memory" and retry later.

  esp_codec_dev.c   check set_fmt's return in esp_codec_dev_open()

Apply from the project directory after `idf.py reconfigure` has populated
managed_components (patches/apply_patches.sh does this and is idempotent):
    patch -p1 -d managed_components/espressif__esp_codec_dev < patches/0002-esp_codec_dev-1.5.11-fail-open-when-set_fmt-fails.patch

Upstream: https://components.espressif.com/components/espressif/esp_codec_dev/versions/1.5.11
          https://github.com/espressif/esp-adf/tree/master/components/esp_codec_dev
License:  Apache-2.0 (upstream); this modification is offered under the same terms.
Author:   this repository's author (github.com/revoltn), 2026-09-02. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

diff -ruN a/esp_codec_dev.c b/esp_codec_dev.c
--- a/esp_codec_dev.c
+++ b/esp_codec_dev.c
@@ -176,7 +176,19 @@
     const audio_codec_if_t *codec = dev->codec_if;
     const audio_codec_data_if_t *data_if = dev->data_if;
     if (data_if->set_fmt) {
-        data_if->set_fmt(data_if, dev->dev_caps, fs);
+        /* LOCAL PATCH (bedside_v01, 2026-09-02): upstream ignores this return
+         * value. When the I2S slot reconfig fails (typically ESP_ERR_NO_MEM
+         * allocating DMA descriptors in internal RAM) the channel has been
+         * left with dma.desc == NULL, and the enable() below panics in
+         * i2s_rx_channel_start with a NULL load. Fail the open instead so the
+         * caller can report "codec busy / out of memory" and retry later. */
+        int fmt_ret = data_if->set_fmt(data_if, dev->dev_caps, fs);
+        if (fmt_ret != ESP_CODEC_DEV_OK) {
+            ESP_LOGE(TAG, "Data interface set_fmt failed (%d) - not enabling channel", fmt_ret);
+            dev->input_opened = false;
+            dev->output_opened = false;
+            return ESP_CODEC_DEV_DRV_ERR;
+        }
     }
     if (data_if->enable) {
         data_if->enable(data_if, dev->dev_caps, true);
